WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:16.698
Hi! In an English sentence, the subject and the verb must agree, like good partners. A singular subject takes a singular verb, and a plural subject takes a plural verb. Today we'll learn subject–verb agreement.

2
00:00:16.848 --> 00:00:25.482
One subject: the verb takes s. The dog barks. More than one: no s. The dogs bark.

3
00:00:25.632 --> 00:00:32.970
The same goes for be and have. Singular subjects take is and has, plural subjects take are and have.

4
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:45.738
Two people joined by and make a plural subject: My sister and I are going to the library. Uncountable nouns like water and milk take a singular verb: the milk is cold.

5
00:00:45.888 --> 00:00:53.730
Each, every, everyone and nobody are singular. Each of the pupils has a name tag. Everyone is excited.

6
00:00:53.880 --> 00:01:01.626
In the box of crayons, the real subject is box, one box, so we use is. The crayons after of don't count.

7
00:01:01.776 --> 00:01:08.634
With there is and there are, look at the noun that follows. A cat takes is. Many fish takes are.

8
00:01:08.784 --> 00:01:18.066
With neither… nor and either… or, the verb agrees with the nearer subject. Here it is pupils, plural, so we use know.

9
00:01:18.216 --> 00:01:24.210
Watch out! Seeing boys and thinking the subject is plural is a common mistake!

10
00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:30.810
In each of the boys, the real subject is each, meaning every single one. It is singular.

11
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.706
So we say: Each of the boys has a ball.

12
00:01:35.856 --> 00:01:45.762
Your turn! The box of crayons, ___, on the shelf. Is or are? Pause and think.

13
00:01:45.912 --> 00:01:53.010
Is. The subject is box, which is one box. Did you get it right?

14
00:01:53.160 --> 00:02:03.210
Another one! There, ___, many fish in the pond. Is or are? Pause and think.

15
00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:13.410
Are. Many fish means more than one fish, so it is plural. The plural of fish is still fish. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:24.498
Next one! Neither the teacher nor the pupils, ___, the answer. Know or knows? Pause and think.

17
00:02:24.648 --> 00:02:38.322
Know. The subject nearer the verb is the pupils, which is plural, so there is no s. If we turned it round, neither the pupils nor the teacher, we would use knows. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:38.472 --> 00:02:48.450
Last one! Everyone in the class, ___, excited. Is or are? Pause and think.

19
00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:56.490
Is. Everyone is about many people, but in grammar it is singular. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:05.346
Remember: find the real subject first. Singular takes is, has, or a verb with s. Plural takes are and have.

21
00:03:05.496 --> 00:03:15.714
Each and everyone are singular. A and B is plural. There is or there are depends on the noun after it. Neither… nor follows the nearer subject.

22
00:03:15.864 --> 00:03:21.522
Next time you write, check that your subject and verb agree!

